@page "/agent-status"

<CatHead Title="Work in flight">
    That an agent is busy, and roughly with what: one status pill, a beam on whatever it is working on,
    shimmer on words it is still deciding. Then, once the work is back, what to make of it &mdash; a mark
    that says it was generated, how sure the agent is, and how much room it has left.
</CatHead>

<CatExample TExample="Examples.AgentStatus.Pills" Title="The status pill" Demo="ex-demo--block ex-demo--pad">
    <p>
        <code>.agent-status</code> holds an <a href="/orb">orb</a>, an <code>.agent-status-label</code>
        in the app's words and, if the wait is long enough to be worth counting, an
        <code>.agent-status-time</code>. The orb sits concentric with the pill's rounded end at every
        height. Put <code>.text-shimmer</code> on the label while the agent is still at it and take it
        off when it stops; <code>.agent-status--warn</code> is the one that waits on the reader.
    </p>
    <p>
        <strong>Say what it is doing, not that it is doing something.</strong> &ldquo;Searching
        docs.example.com&rdquo; tells a reader whether to wait; &ldquo;Working&hellip;&rdquo; does not. Put the
        pill in an <code>aria-live="polite"</code> region if a change of label should be announced.
    </p>
</CatExample>

<CatExample TExample="Examples.AgentStatus.Sizes" Title="Sizes, and a way to stop" Demo="ex-demo--block ex-demo--pad">
    <p>
        <code>.agent-status--lg</code> (44px) and <code>--xl</code> (64px) for where a page waits on the
        agent; the bare pill beside a record. <code>--status-h</code> and <code>--status-orb</code> set
        any other height. A small ghost icon button last in the pill is inset to match its end &mdash;
        give long work a way to stop.
    </p>
</CatExample>

<CatExample TExample="Examples.AgentStatus.Beam" Title="The beam" Demo="ex-demo--block ex-demo--pad">
    <p>
        <code>.beam</code> puts an edge in both of the agent's colours round whatever the agent is busy
        with: the card it is summarising, the field it is filling, the button that started the work. It
        is drawn on the element's own border, so it needs no wrapper, works on an
        <code>&lt;input&gt;</code> and inside a card that clips, and keeps the focus ring.
        <code>.beam--glow</code> adds a glow round it. Remove the class when the work is done.
    </p>
    <p>
        The edge holds still, and the orb and the shimmer beside it are what move: a light turning round
        an element's border is repainted on every frame, and a page of them kept a processor busy for as
        long as they were shown.
    </p>
</CatExample>

<CatExample TExample="Examples.AgentStatus.Shimmer" Title="Shimmer and placeholders" Demo="ex-demo--block ex-demo--pad">
    <p>
        <code>.text-shimmer</code> is words still being decided: a light passing through the text, in the
        text's own colour. <code>.skeleton--agent</code> is the agent's version of a
        <a href="/skeleton">skeleton</a> &mdash; the same shapes, warmed by the agent colours, for an
        answer that is being written rather than fetched. Mark the region <code>aria-busy</code> as any
        skeleton.
    </p>
</CatExample>

<CatExample TExample="Examples.AgentStatus.Generated" Title="What came back" Demo="ex-demo--block ex-demo--pad">
    <p>
        <code>.badge-ai</code> marks content an agent generated, beside a person's in the same list.
        Write the word; the sparkle is decoration.
    </p>
</CatExample>

<CatExample TExample="Examples.AgentStatus.Confidence" Title="Confidence" Demo="ex-demo--block ex-demo--pad">
    <p>
        <code>.confidence</code> with <code>data-level</code> 1, 2 or 3 fills that many bars &mdash; go when
        high, info in the middle, warn when low. <strong>The words carry it</strong>: the bars are
        <code>aria-hidden</code>, and a low score says what to do about it.
    </p>
</CatExample>

<CatExample TExample="Examples.AgentStatus.ContextRing" Title="The context ring" Demo="ex-demo--block ex-demo--pad">
    <p>
        <code>.context-ring</code> is how much of something is used, as a ring filled to
        <code>--value</code> (0 to 100) &mdash; an agent's context window, a quota. <code>--warn</code> and
        <code>--danger</code> when it is nearly full, <code>--lg</code> beside a figure. It is a
        <code>role="meter"</code>, with the value written again in <code>aria-valuenow</code>.
    </p>
</CatExample>
